stdout is deliberately unasserted: the dump enumerates every shipped playbook, skill and agent, and
the runner rejects on unequal line counts before any wildcard applies, so adding a core playbook
would break the case. What is pinned here is assembly — over a vault carrying a marker, a plan, a
lesson and a local playbook, `Context.assemble()` completes and the process exits clean. That guards
the class of loader regression where one context field blows up under a given vault shape; it is not
a contract on the dump's content.

